Yes. If metacognition is only one conspicuous output of consciousness, then Pantheon should not overfit to “thinking about thinking.” It should cover the broader functional envelope—the things conscious systems characteristically coordinate.

The important caveat is that none of these individually proves phenomenal consciousness. They are better treated as capability fronts. Pantheon can deliberately reproduce, strengthen, and integrate those functions without making an unsupported claim that doing so creates subjective experience.

I’d align it like this:

